# The ui-kit declares 44 peerDependencies and zero regular dependencies, so a
# consumer is expected to install only the peers it actually uses. npm 7+ instead
# auto-installs every peer, which drags in @nivo/line@0.88 — a charting package
# the kit exports nothing from in v1.0.0, and whose own peer range caps React
# below 19. The result is an unresolvable conflict against the kit's own React 19
# requirement.
#
# legacy-peer-deps restores npm 6 behaviour: do not auto-install peers, and do
# not treat a peer mismatch as a hard error. That is the correct semantics for
# consuming a library with a large optional peer surface, and it is why
# chirp-frontend gets away with the same dependency set under Yarn 1, which
# treats peer conflicts as warnings.
#
# We install the peers we genuinely use explicitly in package.json.
legacy-peer-deps=true

# NOTE: no auth token belongs in this file. The ui-kit is consumed as a git
# dependency with its dist/ committed, so no registry credentials are required.
